It's all chaos theory. Things that are random have tantalizing bits of
appearances of order. Things happen in runs; a string of good luck, a
string of bad luck. Nethack is simply too long a game for any
particular streak to last throughout. But an early string of bad luck
will simply kill off your character, and you start a new one without
thinking about it. An early string of good luck, on the other hand,
brings thoughts of "this character could be ascendable"; we claim the
ascension, in some sense, and then feel robbed when we don't make it.

Plus, there's the simple human penchant for taking credit for things
that go well. We like to believe it's due to skill. When things go
badly, however, it's not due to bad play; it's that nasty mean
omnipotent horrid RNG out to get us again!

